{ Time for grown up tactics. First trick: pull the guard away from its job. Take on d seven. [%cal Yd2d7][%csl Rc8,Ra8] } 18... Nd7 19. Rxd7 { His queen is the only thing guarding the rook on a eight. Now she must take. [%cal Rc8a8] } (19. Bd4 { A lovely square for the bishop, but the guard keeps her job. } 19... Bf6 20. h3 h6 21. a4 Bxd4 { A level game, and the trick has gone. }) (19. Bd6 { You trade bishops and forget the deflection. } 19... Bxd6 20. Rxd6 Rb8 21. Qe4 Qc7 { Equal. Nothing happened here. }) 19... Qxd7 { She had to take, and now nobody is watching a eight. [%csl Ra8] } 20. Qxa8+ { A whole rook. Deflection: give the guard something it cannot refuse. } (20. Bxg7 { A free pawn while a rook hangs in the corner. } 20... Rd8 21. Bh6 Qd4 22. g3 Qf6 { You gave a rook for a knight and got nothing. }) (20. h4 { A quiet move, and the whole point disappears. } 20... Rd8 21. a3 f6 22. Bf4 b5 { The rook walked away and you are worse. }) 1-0


