{ He has just brought the rook to e one to guard it. Can you pull that guard away? } 24. Rae1 Bxf2+ { The bishop offers itself with check. The rook has no choice. } (24... Qh5 { A natural retreat, and the moment is gone. } 25. Re5 Bd4 26. Rf5 Qh3 { He is completely fine now. }) (24... Qf3 { You keep the queen active, and he simply defends. } 25. Be3 Bxe3 26. Rxe3 Qb7 { Nothing left of your attack. }) (24... Qg4 { A trade offer that throws the whole thing away. } 25. Qxg4 Nxg4 26. Bf5 Nxf2 { Now you are the one losing material. }) 25. Rxf2 Qxe1+ { The guard is on f two now, so e one is free. Check, and a rook. } (25... Qxf2+ { The wrong rook. That one has the king behind it. } 26. Kxf2 h6 27. Bf5 Rf8 { You gave your queen away for a rook. }) (25... Qa6 { You save the queen and lose the point. } 26. Bxf6 Qxa4 27. Bxa4 gxf6 { A dull ending instead of a win. }) 0-1


