{ He has just blocked with the knight, and only his queen is guarding it. } 14. Nd2 e5 { A little pawn attacks the queen. Even a pawn can be the deflector. [%cal Ge5d4] } (14... Rd8 { A useful looking rook move, and the chance has gone. } 15. Bf3 Qa6 16. e4 e5 { Now the push comes too late. }) (14... Qh5 { The queen steps aside and he untangles. } 15. Nf3 Qg4 16. Qxg4 Nxg4 { A level game. }) (14... Qg4 { You offer a trade with something much better available. } 15. f4 Bd7 16. Nf3 Rfd8 { Nothing gained. }) 15. Qxe5 Qxd2 { She had to take the pawn, and the knight was left alone. } (15... Re8 { You chase the queen instead of taking the knight. } 16. Qd4 Bf5 17. a5 Rac8 { The knight escaped and the win with it. }) (15... Bg4 { A pin looks clever, but the knight was free. } 16. Qd4 Bf5 17. h3 Rfd8 { He has consolidated. }) 0-1


