{ He offers a queen trade. Do not take it. Ask what his rook is doing first. } 21... Qb7 22. Rd8+ { You go to the square his rook is guarding. He has to take. [%csl Rb8] } (22. Qxb7 { You take the queen, and the rook takes back for free. } 22... Rxb7 23. Bd4 Be7 24. a4 O-O { All that is left is a level endgame. }) (22. Bd4 { A nice square, but he grabs your queen first. } 22... Qxf3 23. gxf3 Nd5 24. Rfe1 Kd7 { You lost the thread and the game. }) 22... Rxd8 { The rook has left b eight. What was it guarding over there? } 23. Qxb7 { The queen is yours. Pull the guard, then take what it was guarding. } (23. Bxd8 { The wrong capture, and his queen takes yours. } 23... Qxf3 24. gxf3 Kxd8 25. Rd1+ Kc7 { From winning to worse in one move. }) (23. Qxf6 { A knight instead of a queen. } 23... gxf6 24. Bxd8 Kxd8 25. Rd1+ Kc7 { Count before you take. }) 1-0


