{ He has just taken on f three. There is a lonely rook sitting in the corner. } 10. Qxf3 Bxb2 { The bishop walks in. The rook on a one has nowhere safe to go. [%csl Ra1] } (10... O-O { Safe and sensible, but the rook was there for the taking. } 11. Nc3 Re8 12. Bc4 Qd6 { A normal game. }) (10... Nd7 { You develop, and he defends the corner. } 11. c3 O-O 12. Nd2 Rb8 { The chance has gone. }) 11. Qb3 Bxa1 { The rook is yours. A piece with no squares is a piece you can win. } (11... Be5 { You save the bishop and forget the rook. } 12. c3 O-O 13. Nd2 Nd7 { The rook escaped. }) (11... Bf6 { The bishop retreats with a rook on offer. } 12. c3 O-O 13. Nd2 Nd7 { You had a whole rook. }) (11... Qf6 { You defend, and he grabs on b seven. } 12. Qxb7 O-O 13. Qxa8 Bxa1 { A much smaller catch. }) 0-1


