{ He has just taken your knight, and his queen is a long way from home. } 15... bxa4 16. b4 { The pawn takes her squares away. She has exactly one place to go. [%csl Ra5] } (16. Rb1 { You defend the pawn, and she escapes with the knight. } 16... axb3 17. Rxb3 e5 18. Bh2 Ne4 { A piece down for nothing. }) (16. Bg3 { A quiet bishop move while a piece hangs. } 16... axb3 17. Qxb3 e5 18. Qb4 Qc7 { You are simply a knight behind. }) 16... Qb5 17. Bxb5 { Her only square was guarded. A queen for a bishop. } (17. Bd6 { A fancy move with the queen there for the taking. } 17... exd6 18. Bxb5 cxb5 19. Rc1 Rfe8 { You gave a bishop away for nothing. }) (17. Bc7 { You chase the rook and let her out. } 17... Qb7 18. Bxd8 Rxd8 19. f4 Qc7 { A rook, when a queen was waiting. }) 1-0
